===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q1073}}The control center of the [[central nervous system]] of an [[animal]] located in the [[skull]] which is responsible for [[perception]], [[cognition]], [[attention]], [[memory]], [[emotion]], and [[action]].
#: {{syn|en|encephalon|harns|Thesaurus:brain}}
#* {{RQ:De Mornay Sidney Golding Trewnesse|chapter=That there is but Onely One God|page=18|passage=The Ueynes are ſpred foorth throughout the whole bodie, howbeit from one welhead, that is to ſay from the Liuer: ſo be the Sinews, howbeit from the '''Brayne'''; So likewiſe are the Heartſtrings, howbeit from the Heart.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-07-19|author=Ian Sample|volume=189|issue=6|page=34|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly|title=Irregular bedtimes may affect children's brains|url=http://www.theguardian.com/lifeandstyle/2013/jul/08/irregular-bedtimes-affect-childrens-brains|passage=Irregular bedtimes may disrupt healthy '''brain''' development in young children, according to a study of intelligence and sleeping habits.&nbsp; &para;&nbsp;Going to bed at a different time each night affected girls more than boys, but both fared worse on mental tasks than children who had a set bedtime, researchers found.}}
## A part of the brain, especially associated with particular mental functions, abilities, etc.
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1892|author=Benjamin Ward Richardson|title= The Asclepiad|location=London|page=357|text=The left '''brain''', or that which supplies and animates the right side of the body, is the most active '''brain''', as a general rule.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1981|author=w:William Irwin Thompson|title=The Time Falling Bodies Take to Light: Mythology, Sexuality and the Origins of Culture|publisher=Rider/Hutchinson & Co.|location=London|page=113|passage=What is expressed in the lotus, the plumed serpent, or the staff of Osiris is the yogi's knowledge of the three '''brains''' of man. The first '''brain''' is the reptilian '''brain''' of the spinal cord, the '''brain''' of instinctive reflexes, the '''brain''' of the subconscious.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} [[mind|Mind]].
#: {{ux|en|I have too much on my '''brain''' today.}}
#* {{RQ:Tennyson In Memoriam|XIV|22|And I should tell him all my pain, / ⁠And how my life had droop’d of late, / ⁠And he should sorrow o’er my state / And marvel what possess’d my '''brain'''; […]}}
# {{lb|en|in the plural}} [[intellect|Intellect]].
#* '''2008 Quaker Action''' (magazine) ''Rights trampled in rush to deport immigrant workers'', Fall 2008, Vol. 89, No. 3, p. 8:
#*: "We provided a lot of '''brains''' and a lot of heart to the response when it was needed," says Sandra Sanchez, director of AFSC's Immigrants' Voice Program in Des Moines.
#: {{ux|en|She has a lot of '''brains'''.}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} An [[intelligent]] person.
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:genius}}
#: {{ux|en|She was a total '''brain'''.}}
#* {{quote-video game|en|developer=w:BioWare|title={{w|Mass Effect: Andromeda}}|genre=[[science fiction|Science Fiction]]|location=Redwood City|publisher=Electronic Arts|year=2017|system=PC|scene=Nexus|oclc=1261299044|text=Peebee: The '''brains''' and I are comparing Remnant notes and filling in the blanks.}}
## {{lb|en|plurale tantum}} A person who provides the intelligence required for something.
##: {{ux|en|He is the '''brains''' behind the scheme.}}
## {{lb|en|in the singular}} An intellectual or mental [[capacity]].
##: {{ux|en|Gerald always acts like he doesn't have a '''brain'''.}}
